The 27 selected brands are copied byte-for-byte from the archive's light/
and dark/ directories into png/light/ and png/dark/, keeping upstream names.
Use the -color variant when the package provides it; never tint the artwork.
OpenAI, Anthropic, Grok, Groq, Moonshot, Ollama and TypeSafe AI have no -color
file in either directory's complete archive manifest; their official default
artwork is retained, including light/dark contrast differences.
Other selected brands: Azure, ChatGLM, Claude, Cohere, DeepSeek, Doubao,
Gemini, Gemma, Google, Kimi, Meta, MiniMax, Mistral, OpenRouter, Perplexity, Qwen,
SiliconCloud, Together, Volcengine and Zhipu.

To update, download an explicitly versioned archive from the npm registry,
verify its registry integrity and SHA-256, copy only the selected light/dark
PNG pairs unchanged, and update this notice and the upstream license.
Run go test ./internal/aibrands after changing resources or matching rules.
